<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
    A day already claimed: the same cell as its neighbours, filled, with a tick in it.

    A LAYER-LIST, not a compound drawable on the TextView.

    The tick used to be set in code with setCompoundDrawables(). Android pins
    a left compound drawable to the view's left padding edge and centres only
    the text in what is left, so the tick sat off to one side and no gravity
    could move it. Putting it in the background instead centres it by
    construction, and - the part that matters more - the claimed cell is now
    the SAME box as the six beside it, because it is the same shape with one
    extra layer rather than a differently measured view.

    Cells are a fixed 34dp, so nothing here can change a cell's size.
-->
<layer-list xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <item>
        <shape android:shape="rectangle">
            <solid android:color="@color/xp_accent_deep" />
            <corners android:radius="10dp" />
        </shape>
    </item>

    <item
        android:width="15dp"
        android:height="15dp"
        android:drawable="@drawable/ic_check"
        android:gravity="center" />

</layer-list>
